    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302-a1">

                <pb facs="0464" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg376"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Balfour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        American Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 178793/W/3</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-13">November 13,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to Mr. Page’s Note, No.
                    1272, of the 30th September last, relative to the future boundaries of the
                    Czecho-Slovak State, I am directed by Mr. Secretary Balfour to transmit to you,
                    herewith, a memorandum as to the difficulties with which this question is
                    connected, and to assure you that His Majesty’s Government would be glad to
                    receive any views which the Government of the United States may entertain on the
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State, <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. Graham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
